hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27722","Haddathana Sufyan from Ibrahim ibn Maysara from Amr ibn al-Sharid from Abu Rafi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor is most entitled to his saqab or saqab."
"27723","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Malik who said: Haddathani Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Rafi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a young camel from a man, then camels of the charity camels came to him, so he said: Give him; so they said: We find for him nothing except an excellent four-year-old; he said: Give him, for indeed the best of people are the best of them in repayment."
"27724","Haddathana Yahya from Shuba: Haddathani al-Hakam from Ibn Abi Rafi from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of Banu Makhzum over the charity, so he said: Will you not accompany me so you may gain; he said: I said: Until I mention that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so I mentioned that, and he said: Indeed we, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us, and indeed the freedman of a people is of themselves."
"27725","Haddathana Ibn Numayr who said: Akhbarana Sharik, and Abu al-Nadr who said: Haddathana Sharik from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Ali ibn Husayn from Abu Rafi who said: When Fatima gave birth to Hasan, she said: Shall I not sacrifice for my son with blood; he said: No, but shave his head and give the weight of his hair in silver upon the poor and the Awfadh; and the Awfadh were people of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who were needy in the mosque or in the Suffa; and Abu al-Nadr said: of wariq upon the Awfadh, meaning the people of the Suffa, or upon the poor; so I did that; she said: So when I gave birth to Husayn, I did the like of that."
"27726","Haddathana Waki: Haddathana Sufyan from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid from a man from Abu Rafi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to pray with his hair tied up."
"27727","Haddathana Harun ibn Maruf who said: Haddathana Ibn Wahb who said: Akhbarani Amr that Bukayr told him that al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi told him from Abu Rafi that he said: I was in an expedition once, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and bring me Maymuna; so I said: O Prophet of Allah, indeed I am in the expedition; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not love what I love; I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Go and bring her to me; so I went and brought her to him."
"27728","Haddathana Waki who said: Haddathana Sufyan from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the adhan in the ear of al-Hasan ibn Ali when Fatima bore him."
"27729","Haddathana Yazid: Akhbarana Hammad ibn Salama from Abd al-Rahman from his paternal aunt from Abu Rafi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went round his wives in one night and washed at each woman of them a washing; so I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you had washed one washing; so he said: This is purer and better."
"27730","Haddathana Abu Amir who said: Haddathana Yaqub ibn Muhammad ibn Tahla: Haddathana Abu al-Rijal from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Abu Rafi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to kill the dogs, so I went out killing them, not seeing a dog except that I killed it; then there was a dog circling a house, so I went to kill it, and a person called to me from inside the house: O servant of Allah, what do you want to do; he said: I said: I want to kill this dog; so she said: Indeed I am a neglected woman, and this dog drives the beast away from me and alerts me of the comer; so go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mention that to him; he said: So I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he ordered me to kill it."
"27731","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam who said: Haddathana Sharik from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah from Ali ibn Husayn from his father from Abu Rafi from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he heard the caller to prayer he said the like of what he says, and when he said: Come to prayer, he said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"27732","Haddathana Abu Amir who said: Haddathana Zuhayr from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn Husayn from Abu Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed, he bought two fat horned black-and-white rams; and when he prayed and addressed the people, one of them was brought while he was standing in his prayer place, and he slaughtered it himself with the knife, then said: O Allah, indeed this is for my umma altogether, of those who bore witness to You of oneness and bore witness to me of conveyance; then the other was brought and he slaughtered it himself and said: This is for Muhammad and the family of Muhammad; so he fed both of them altogether to the poor, and he and his family ate of them; so we remained years with no man of Banu Hashim sacrificing, Allah having sufficed him the burden by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the expense."
"27733","Haddathana Zakariya ibn Adi who said: Akhbarana Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Ali ibn al-Husayn, and he mentioned it with its chain and its meaning."
"27734","Haddathana Muawiya who said: Haddathana Abu Ishaq al-Fazari from Ibn Jurayj who said: Haddathani Manbudh, a man of the family of Abu Rafi, from al-Fadl ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rafi from Abu Rafi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Asr, would sometimes go to Banu Abd al-Ashhal and talk until he descended for Maghrib; he said: So Abu Rafi said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hastening to Maghrib, he passed by al-Baqi and said: Uff to you, uff to you, twice; so it weighed upon my mind and I held back, and I thought he meant me; so he said: What is the matter with you, walk; he said: I said: I have committed an offense, O Messenger of Allah; he said: And what is that; I said: You have said uff to me; he said: No, but this is the grave of so-and-so; I sent him as a collector upon Banu so-and-so, and he stole a namira cloak, and now he has been clothed with the like of it of fire."
"27735","Haddathana Harun: Akhbarana Ibn Wahb who said: Akhbarana Ibn Jurayj from Manbudh, a man of the family of Abu Rafi: Akhbarani al-Fadl ibn Ubayd Allah from Abu Rafi, and he mentioned it, except that he said: So that weighed upon my mind; and he said: I said: I have committed an offense; he said: And what is that; he said: I said: You have said uff."
"27736","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Sufyan from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Abi Rafi from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call the adhan in the ear of al-Hasan on the day his mother bore him, with the prayer."
"27737","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid who said: Haddathana Abu Jafar, meaning al-Razi, from Shurahbil from Abu Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A sheep was gifted to him and he put it in the pot; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: What is this, O Abu Rafi; so he said: A sheep gifted to us, O Messenger of Allah, and I cooked it in the pot; so he said: Hand me the foreleg, O Abu Rafi; so I handed him the foreleg; then he said: Hand me the other foreleg; so I handed him the other foreleg; then he said: Hand me the other foreleg; so he said: O Messenger of Allah, a sheep has only two forelegs; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Indeed if you had kept silent you would have kept handing me foreleg after foreleg as long as you kept silent; then he called for water and rinsed his mouth and washed the ends of his fingers, then stood and prayed; then he returned to them and found with them cold meat and ate; then he entered the mosque and prayed and did not touch water."
"27738","Haddathana Zakariya ibn Adi who said: Akhbarani Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil who said: So I asked Ali ibn al-Husayn, and he told me from Abu Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when al-Hasan ibn Ali was born, his mother Fatima wanted to sacrifice for him with two rams, so he said: Do not sacrifice for him, but shave the hair of his head, then give its weight in wariq in the path of Allah; then Husayn was born after that, and she did the like of that."
"27739","Haddathana Affan and Yunus who said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd who said: Haddathana Matar from Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymuna while lawful and consummated with her while lawful, and I was the messenger between them."
"27740","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad who said: Haddathana al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, who said: Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya from Abu Asma, freedman of Banu Jafar, from Abu Rafi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: Indeed there will be a matter between you and Aisha; he said: I, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Yes; he said: I; he said: Yes; he said: Then am I the most wretched of them, O Messenger of Allah; he said: No, but when that happens, return her to her safe place."
